The TypeScript adaptation sizes its delay ring to the largest delay plus one
sample instead of native's power-of-two buffer, reducing each delay modulo the
native buffer size so the output is identical. It accepts only constant
decimal values, the middle_source names or integers and the boolean names or
0/1, refuses inputs native would remix to stereo implicitly, and has no
runtime commands. The original source and full notices remain in the pinned
upstream submodule.
